e middle east  and urges it to help belarus  the root of the problem is the policy  carried out by western countries  including nato and eu member states  regarding the middle east and north  africa over years as they were trying to  impose a western style better life  several people along the border have  already died from exposure there could  be many more to come rory challenge al  jazeera  well dominic kane is following the story  from berlin dominic what have the eu  commission had to say about this  lots of words coming from the european  union from several different officials  not the least of them from the president  of the european commission ursula fond  de la and she says that what's happening  on that border that we saw we're hearing  rory report about there  basically the  instrumentalization of refugees says  president fond airline in other words  that she is accusing the belarusian  government of using these refugees these  migrants as an instrument of foreign  policy president van der lion wants to  have much more sanctions imposed in  belarus and that's the view that other  politicians in other parts of the eu  seem to be endorsing too we know that  here the german government the interior  minister has has effectively endorsed  the polish government's  approach vis-a-vis the uh the safety the  security of the border with belarus the  idea of militarization of the of that  zone of a fence being put there we know  also that the lithuanian government has  said that it is putting everything in  place in order to have and to enact a  state of emergency along its border with  belarus remember that lithuania and  poland have the longest longest borders  with belarus those are the frontiers  which are now the front line of this  hybrid war that we were hearing the  polish government representative refer  to there so from the european  perspective from the eu perspective at  least you have solidarity being  expressed in brussels and in other  member states f